  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nIf I parse a conforming document such as\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<title>Test</title>\n</head>\n<body>\n<select>\n<button><selectedcontent></selectedcontent></button>\n<option><span id=\"foo\">foo</span></option>\n</select>\n</body>\n</html>\n```\n\nupon which the `<option>` contents get cloned into `<selectedcontent>`, and I serialize the result, I get a non-conforming document:\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<title>Test</title>\n</head>\n<body>\n<select>\n<button><selectedcontent><span id=\"foo\">foo</span></selectedcontent></button>\n<option><span id=\"foo\">foo</span></option>\n</select>\n</body>\n</html>\n```\n\nThis violates the `<selectedcontent>` element’s [empty content model](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-elements.html#the-selectedcontent-element), and has also introduced [invalid duplicate `id`s](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#global-attributes:~:text=the%20id%20attribute%20value%20must%20be%20unique). This seems like very odd behavior for the specification to expect of a parser.",
